  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Tamper-Evident Seal",
    "overview": "lockbox is a calm sealing desk. A file goes in, a numbered seal comes out. The ground is a cool pale grey, the work happens on a single white card, and everything is near-black ink except one colour: security-tape blue, the blue of the tape that goes across a parcel to prove nobody opened it. That blue marks the step you are on, the button that moves you forward, and the seal strip laid across each finished file. Red appears only when a seal is broken or something has gone wrong.\n\nThe structure is a guided stepper: a centred title with a one-line promise, an Encrypt | Decrypt toggle, and a vertical three-step stepper with one step open at a time. The density is low and the copy is short. Personality lives in two places only: the treasure-box logo, whose lid closes once when a file is encrypted, and the seal strip with its white mono serial and perforated edge. The rest of the interface stays quiet so those two moments read.\n\nLight and dark themes are full peers. Both follow the system setting and can be forced with the header toggle; every colour token has a dark counterpart.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One accent (tape blue), spent only on the active step, the primary action and seals.",
      "Red is a signal for broken seals, errors and irreversible loss, never decoration.",
      "Archivo for every word of interface; Martian Mono only for data.",
      "A single white card on a grey desk, with one soft ambient shadow.",
      "Gently rounded corners (7px controls, 14px card), 1px hairlines, dashed edges for \"not yet sealed\"."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Tape Rule",
        "body": "Tape blue fills only three things: the active or completed step marker, the step's primary button, and the seal strip. Everything else that needs blue (links, status, notices) uses the text or wash variant, never a solid fill.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Broken Seal Rule",
        "body": "Red means \"this is broken, failed, or cannot be undone\". A torn seal, an error, an invalid field, a weak password, a Private key that must never be shared. It never appears as a brand colour or for emphasis.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Data Face Rule",
        "body": "Martian Mono is for values a person might compare, copy or read aloud: seal numbers, keys, sizes, passwords. Labels, headings, buttons and prose are always Archivo.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Card Rule",
        "body": "A page has one raised surface: the white card. Nothing inside it casts a shadow; inner groups use hairlines or a wash.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** spend solid tape blue only on the current or completed step marker, the step's primary button and the seal strip (The Tape Rule).",
      "**Do** keep one primary button per step, taking the remaining width of its action row.",
      "**Do** set seal numbers, keys, file sizes and passwords in Martian Mono at 13px with tabular figures, and everything else in Archivo.",
      "**Do** use a dashed edge for anything still open or unsealed, and turn it solid once complete.",
      "**Do** give every colour a dark-theme counterpart and check both themes; dark uses the lighter tape-blue-text for blue text.",
      "**Do** keep the page to one centred title, one promise line and one white card.",
      "**Do** show focus with the 3px blue ring plus a transparent outline."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use red for anything that is not broken, failed, invalid or irreversible.",
      "**Don't** fill a whole header band, page background or large area with tape blue; the calm grey ground is part of the look.",
      "**Don't** put Martian Mono on labels, headings or buttons.",
      "**Don't** add shadows inside the card or raise a second surface on the page (The One Card Rule).",
      "**Don't** spread the treasure box beyond the header logo and the one results chest with its single lid-closing animation.",
      "**Don't** reuse the seal-kind legend style (10px tracked capitals) outside the seal strip; it is the tape's printing, not a heading style."
    ]
  }
